capability open-api-estate-stream
intent: Subscribe to the estate's live feed, the legacy observer's publish/subscribe channel: every run the hosting facade executes is published into it, and any signed-in session subscribes from any machine (GET /events, as the observer served it, and /sfx/v1/estate-execution/stream). The session store confirms the caller session, and the answer instructs the facade to stream the feed as server-sent events: the opening frame, the replay, the replay end, then each new event as a run writes it, framed by project-api-estate-events, keep-alive comments while quiet, until the session expires or a recheck through check-api-session, at the given interval, cannot confirm it. The selectors are the observer's: since (or Last-Event-ID) replays after that sequence; run=current or last replays the most recent run and keeps to it, narrowed by graphId to the most recent run that captured that graph; run=<n> does the same for the nth retained run; run=next waits for the next run and keeps to it; without since or run only new events arrive. A run selector or since the observer refused is refused as it did, 400 invalid_run or invalid_since. The x-observer-instance header names the feed, so a client knows when a restart began a new sequence.
outcome: a host directive (application/vnd.sfx.host-directive+json) stream-estate with the cursor, the run selection, the projection, the frames and the session; a 400 invalid_run or invalid_since; or EVIDENCE_SESSION_REQUIRED
inquiry: May this caller watch the estate's live feed, and from where?
input contract open-api-estate-stream-request.v1 {"type":"object"}
output contract open-api-estate-stream-result.v1 {"type":"object"}
cli display outcome as json
scenario open-api-estate-stream root terminal
given: the caller principal and session, and the observer's optional since, run and graphId
when: the session store reads the caller session
then: the outcome is the stream directive, the selector refusal, or EVIDENCE_SESSION_REQUIRED
operation open-api-estate-stream.read-prepare kind invoke-port port open-api-estate-stream-read-prepare
operation open-api-estate-stream.read kind invoke-port port open-api-estate-stream-read
operation open-api-estate-stream.answer kind invoke-port port open-api-estate-stream-answer
platform bind open-api-estate-stream-read-prepare
platform: sda-authority-transformation-port.v1
config: {"expression":{"op":"object","fields":{"executionTarget":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"executionNamespace":{"op":"literal","value":"sidefx:capabilities"},"executionScenario":{"op":"literal","value":"sql-database-reader"},"inputType":{"op":"literal","value":"json"},"dispatchRequest":{"op":"object","fields":{"dataSource":{"op":"literal","value":"sfx-identity-database"},"statement":{"op":"literal","value":"SET NOCOUNT ON; DECLARE @principal_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.principalId')); DECLARE @session_id uniqueidentifier = TRY_CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.sessionId')); DECLARE @expires datetimeoffset(7) = (SELECT s.expires_at FROM [identity].session s JOIN [identity].principal p ON p.principal_id = s.principal_id WHERE s.session_id = @session_id AND s.principal_id = @principal_id AND s.revoked_at IS NULL AND s.expires_at > SYSUTCDATETIME() AND p.active = 1); SELECT (SELECT JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.since') AS since, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.run') AS run, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.graphId') AS graphId, LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), @principal_id)) AS principalId, LOWER(CONVERT(varchar(36), @session_id)) AS sessionId, @expires AS sessionExpiresAt, CONVERT(bit, CASE WHEN @expires IS NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END) AS sessionLive, COALESCE(TRY_CONVERT(int, JSON_VALUE(@input, '$.recheckMilliseconds')), 5000) AS recheckMilliseconds FOR JSON PATH, WITHOUT_ARRAY_WRAPPER, INCLUDE_NULL_VALUES) AS value;"},"resultColumn":{"op":"literal","value":"value"},"input":{"op":"path","path":""}}}}}}
